ore  yeah well that's the billion dollar  question so last night or not last night  yesterday afternoon the police services  board met they heard from the new  interim chief that's a steve bell he was  deputy police chief before  every single member is asking him what's  the plan what's the plan what's the plan  uh and uh the interim chief bell is says  that there is a plan he promises that  ottawa police have a plan they're  working on it they're working to refine  it and he'll let the police services  board know uh behind closed doors you  know when it's ready to activate because  he doesn't want to give  information publicly about that plan but  again this is day 20 and a lot of people  frustrated uh that that this is the  point that things are at right now and  and with the police chief gone a lot of  questions about you know how that that  leadership vacuum will fill in and what  will happen we heard from the public  safety minister uh yesterday talking  about the integrated command center and  he was suggesting that opp ontario  provincial police and the rcmp with this  new structure with the integrated  command center between the three of them  that those police forces are in a  position to command and control uh as  well so still waiting for details in  terms of how this all plays out i will  point out that there has not been a  media opportunity to ask ottawa police  any questions since friday we are  wednesday now we are expecting to hear  uh from council late this afternoon okay  so you you point out the leadership  questions when it comes to the police  service but a lot of questions and  criticism of the leadership at all  levels of government they are not immune  to this and of course to be continued on  that but in terms of today what more do  we expect  uh a few things so you'll remember uh  perhaps view viewers will remember the  honking  and how there was a court injunction in  place that called for an end to the  honking we've you know seen occasional  honking but nothing like those first  days where it was just non-stop and and  people were not sleeping for days uh on  end uh and so those lawyers are back in  court today because the court granted a  10-day injunction that's set to expire  lawyers will argue  to extend that for the resident's sake  here in the city so we're watching that  today we're watching as i mentioned uh  the council meeting this afternoon we  haven't heard from the mayor uh  in a number of days either so looking  for an update there and then of course  watching to see if anything develops on  the hill in terms of uh when the  emergencies act will be tabled and and  some debate to get underway
 

